# Required Functionality

1. The script should reference a designated floor activation pad.

2. When a player steps on the pad, the trap should activate.

3. The pad should begin flashing between two configurable colors to warn nearby players.

4. The flashing should occur for a configurable warning period before the ceiling falls.

5. After the warning period, the spike ceiling should drop downward toward a designated endpoint.

6. The ceiling should move smoothly and visibly.

7. If a player is caught underneath the falling ceiling or touches the active spikes, they should receive configurable damage or instant death.

8. The ceiling should remain at its lowest position for a configurable amount of time.

9. After the delay, the ceiling should return to its original position.

10. The activation pad should stop flashing and return to its original appearance once the trap resets.

11. The trap should have an activation cooldown.

12. Multiple players stepping on the pad during an active sequence must not restart or duplicate the trap sequence.

## Required Changes you may have to make

• Activation pad.
• Ceiling model (Or empty space above).
• Starting position.
• Falling distance.
• Movement speed.
• Warning duration.
• Flashing interval.
• Warning color.
• Normal pad color.
• Damage amount or Instant-death.
• Time spent at the bottom.
• Reset speed.
• Activation cooldown.

# Please Notice
## Server Security

Use server-controlled movement to ensure all players see the same animation.

Preserve the ceiling model’s orientation and move all connected parts together.

Make sure the ceiling does not fall through the floor or move beyond its configured endpoint.

All activation detection, animations, damage, and trap resets must happen on the server. (Do not use LocalScripts or client-controlled RemoteEvents.)
